sequenceDiagram
    participant P as Party
    participant J as Jurors (3/5/7)
    participant A as Admin Keeper
    participant DB as Database

    Note over P,DB: Phase 1 — Evidence (48h)
    P->>DB: POST /disputes (open dispute)
    A->>DB: POST /disputes/:id/assign-jurors

    Note over P,DB: Phase 2 — Commit (24h)
    J->>DB: POST /disputes/:id/vote/commit<br/>commitHash = keccak256(id, vote, salt)

    Note over P,DB: Phase 3 — Reveal (24h)
    A->>DB: POST /disputes/:id/advance<br/>(when deadline or >50% committed)
    J->>DB: POST /disputes/:id/vote/reveal<br/>(vote, salt) verified against commit

    Note over P,DB: Phase 4 — Resolution
    A->>DB: POST /disputes/:id/advance<br/>(when deadline or >50% revealed)
    DB->>DB: tallyVotes → majority wins
    alt Majority freelancer
        DB->>DB: splitBps = 10000 → payout to freelancer
    else Majority client
        DB->>DB: splitBps = 0 → refund to client
    else Tie
        DB->>DB: tie_escalated → admin arbiter sets splitBps
    end
    DB->>DB: write ledger entries<br/>(release + fee + juror rewards/slashing)
